To  prevent  malicious  access, implements a simple address‐based
access control.  With or specified by  will  avoid  relaying  un‐
wanted  traffic.   The  configuration file contains directives of
the following format: If the source address of  a  query  matches
and  the  translated destination address matches deny the connec‐
tion.  If the source address of a query matches  and  the  trans‐
lated destination address matches permit the connection.  The di‐
rectives  are evaluated in sequence, and the first matching entry
will be effective.  If there is no match the traffic will be  de‐
nied.   With  inetd mode, traffic may be filtered by using access
control functionality in exits with on  success,  and  on  error.
